aising lead, while Matt Dunlap has held narrow advantages in most recent polls, though several were commissioned by Democratic groups. An independent University of New Hampshire survey also showed Dunlap ahead in September.\n\nRatings from national analysts tilt narrowly toward LePage, with five outlets calling the race Lean Republican and two calling it Lean Democratic. Prediction markets disagree with each other, and LePage's part-time residency in Florida has featured prominently in the final debates alongside exchanges over Social Security. The combination of Dunlap's thin polling lead and the district's Republican lean leaves this among the closest House races in the country, with a slight Republican edge.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.4239, "margin": -1.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.38, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3812, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.377, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.3179, "margin": -2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.4062, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.4214, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.437, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.4556, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.4353, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.4338, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.4042, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.4713, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.3776, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.3456, "margin": -2.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.3722, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.4333, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.4085, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.406, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.3777, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.4678, "margin": -1.0}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.408, "margin": -1.5}, {"date": "2026-1